H1("IX. DISCUSSION")
H2("A. Relation to Prior Work")
BP("Ssense and APLiance agree on necessity of automating DPDP compliance and decomposing legal provisions into decision gates. Key differentiators: (1) Open-Weights vs. Proprietary API -- APLiance relies on zero-shot prompting of a closed commercial API; Ssense trains and releases an open-weights Law-LM. (2) Statutory Coverage -- APLiance operationalizes 7 provisions; Ssense covers a 26-node tree spanning the full DPDP Act, 2023 and Rules, 2025 including Schedules. (3) Epistemology of Silence -- APLiance penalizes silence universally; Ssense applies a formal three-step deductive chain conditioned on deontic modality. (4) CFG Decoding -- XGrammar pushdown automaton eliminates brittle regex-based parsing. (5) False Positive Rate -- Ssense achieves 0.00% FPR vs. APLiance's implicit ~100%. (6) Serving Infrastructure -- APLiance lacks a production serving architecture; Ssense provides PagedAttention + S-LoRA + XGrammar + multi-tier caching.")
H2("B. Architectural Rationale: Neuro-Symbolic Synthesis")
BP("The neural SLM and deterministic SCL exhibit complementary failure modes. The SLM can miss explicit clauses under long-context attention decay, or hallucinate from silence. The SCL cannot overlook explicit violations it is parameterized to capture but lacks semantic context for novel phrasings. The union V_final = V_SLM union V_SCL bounds semantic breadth with deterministic legal guardrails: omission firewall suppresses false positives from neural inference on silence; SCL prevents false negatives from neural attention failure; safe-harbor lookarounds prevent spurious regex flags on protected retention.")
H2("C. Data Sovereignty and Open-Weights Release")
BP("Submitting corporate disclosures to closed proprietary APIs introduces data sovereignty violations and jurisdictional leakage. Ssense preserves sovereignty: Ssense-DPDP-7B released as standalone merged BF16 safetensors, enabling offline execution with full auditability. Inference server stores only SHA-256 policy hashes and structured audit JSON, guaranteeing zero persistence of raw policy text.")
H2("D. Epistemic Conservatism and Fairness to Fiduciaries")
BP("False positive citations create legal vulnerabilities and unjust reputational harm to compliant entities. Ssense enforces epistemic conservatism: silent practices are filtered by the omission firewall; legitimate safe harbors preserved by SCL lookarounds; SimPO length-normalized margin penalizes over-calling. FPR=0.00% ensures every citation is anchored in verifiable statutory evidence, establishing an objective foundation for human regulatory review.")
