H1("X. LIMITATIONS AND THREATS TO VALIDITY")
BP("Sample Size: The fiduciary pilot evaluated ten market-leading Indian platforms, which may exhibit higher compliance maturity than smaller commercial websites, potentially understating violation prevalence across long-tail operators.")
BP("Ground Truth Methodology: Gold-standard labels established via dual independent legal specialist annotations (Cohen's kappa=0.884, p<0.001). Expanding annotation panels across diverse legal jurisdictions and India-specific regulatory contexts will further strengthen inter-rater ground truth.")
BP("Statutory Cross-Clause Interplay: Some violations involve composite breaches spanning multiple sections (e.g., Swiggy's indefinite retention spans S.8(7) and S.4(1)). Formalizing multi-label dependency graphs across interlocking statutory obligations represents active research.")
BP("Document Truncation: The web crawler enforces a 64,000-character cap, truncating outlier policies. Processing ultra-long policies without truncation requires distributed memory management. Statutory Evolution: The knowledge base reflects the DPDP Act, 2023 and Rules, 2025 as notified. Amendments will require re-indexing. Vernacular Scope: DOM normalization filters non-Latin scripts; Eighth Schedule language evaluation deferred to Study E6. Legal Disclaimer: Ssense outputs do not constitute formal legal counsel.")
