BP("Ssense introduces Ssense-DPDP-7B, the first domain-adapted Legal Small Language Model and scalable serving architecture for auditing global web compliance under India's DPDP Act, 2023 and DPDP Rules, 2025. Combining rsLoRA fine-tuning and SimPO alignment on an open-weights base with a formal 26-node deontic violation taxonomy, a three-step omission firewall, and a neuro-symbolic SCL backstop (V_final = V_SLM union V_SCL), Ssense bridges sovereign statutory texts and automated compliance auditing. PagedAttention continuous batching, KV pre-warming, and speculative decoding deliver TTFT P50: 420-1,120 ms and memory-safe execution at B=16 (312.8 tokens/s, 14.8 GB VRAM).")
